{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiEllipticFreedom","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiEllipticFreedom","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiEllipticFreedom.faddeevPhi_mul_elliptic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevPhiEllipticFreedom.faddeevPhi_mul_elliptic","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevPhiEllipticFreedom.lean#L39-L67","doc":"**Elliptic freedom.** If `e` is elliptic with respect to the period lattice\n`⟨ib, i/b⟩`, then `e · Φ` is again a `FaddeevPhi` solution: the elliptic factor\n`e(z ∓ ·)` agrees across each quasi-period shift and cancels the prefactor\nmismatch. Hence the class does not determine `Φ`'s divisor — a nonconstant\nelliptic `e` produces a solution with a different divisor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}